  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 205 PM CST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nSunday night through Friday:\n\nCold advection on nwly winds will continue into Mon evening as\nanother shortwave trough tracks across the nrn Great Lakes on \nMon. High pressure will then likely remain in the vicinity of \nsrn WI for the remainder of the week with temps returning to\nnear normal. There is some uncertainty with the evolution of an\nelongated n-s shortwave trough that crosses the Rockies into the\ncentral USA. The GEFS and mean ECMWF suggest the srn portion of\nthe wave will likely amplify Wed-Thu over the lower MS River\nValley with much less troughing to the north. Thus much of the\nextended forecast is dry. \n\nGehring",
